              "The possibility of renewed high-level talks comes as the trade war between the world’s top two economies appears set to intensify. Trump said last week that new tariffs on $200 billion of Chinese goods could go into effect “very soon” and warned that another, even bigger wave of measures is “ready to go on short notice if I want.”",
              "Trump’s top economic adviser, Larry Kudlow, said Wednesday on Fox Business that the US government had received information that “the top of the Chinese government wished to pursue talks.” He said Treasury Secretary Steven Mnuchin had sent an invitation.\n\nKudlow declined to provide further details on the potential talks. The Wall Street Journal reported earlier Wednesday that Mnuchin had sent the offer to a group of Chinese officials led by Vice Premier Liu He, the top economic adviser to President Xi Jinping",
